    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on capitalizing on favorable matchups against mid-tier rotations, with **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (68.19) leading the charge as our strongest plays. **Dylan Beavers** benefits immensely from a massive +16% park factor boost and a prime leadoff spot, making him a high-upside play against L\u00f3pez. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** provides stability at shortstop; his score is buoyed by a +17% SP skill advantage against Mikolas and a +8% order bonus. **Bryce Harper** (67.44) and **Taylor Ward** (64.51) remain locked in as core producers, with **Taylor Ward** mirroring **Dylan Beavers**\u2019 park-driven ceiling, though he faces a slightly tougher path to runs given his #4 spot compared to the leadoff roles of others.\n\nWe have strategically avoided the trap of starting marginal pieces against elite arms, which forced the difficult decision to bench **JJ Bleday** (46.72). While **JJ Bleday** was our closest consideration for a slot, he ultimately lost out due to a -14% penalty in dynamic platoon matchups, leaving him beneath the efficiency threshold required to displace starters like **Gavin Sheets** or **Daulton Varsho**. We are keeping a close watch on **Bryce Harper**, as his status remains \"Lineup Pending\"; should he be held out, we will need to pivot to the bench. Furthermore, while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (52.96) remains a roster staple, his score is currently compressed by a -15% SP skill penalty against Rasmussen, signaling a high-risk day for our anchor hitter.",
